# Space Fury sound board -- netlist converted from MAME
#
# Sega/Gremlin G-80 games carry a sound board of their own, driven from the CPU board's
# output ports: the port bits arrive here as ports (MAME's TTL_INPUT names, HI_D0 ...
# LO_D7 or SOUND_0 ...), and the mixed sound goes out to the amplifier.
#
# Source: MAME mame0289 (commit f34f02505e32), src/mame/sega/nl_spacfury.cpp,
# NETLIST_START(spacfury). Licence CC0-1.0 by the file's own header (line 1),
# copyright-holders Aaron Giles (line 2).
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mamedev/mame/mame0289/src/mame/sega/nl_spacfury.cpp
# Converted by tools/mame_netlist.py; checked by tools/build_board_nets.py.
#
# What the conversion means. MAME's netlists are written to be simulated, so this is a
# second reading of the sheet by someone else, not a read of it: designators and pin
# numbers are MAME's unless the notes say the sheet was read to correct them. Names on
# `label` lines are MAME's, which mostly follow the sheet's with Q for an overbar; `net`
# is used only for the supply rails. A `port` is a net that leaves what this file
# describes -- a signal from the CPU or the other board, a cabinet control, or a source
# MAME simulates with a stand-in rather than the circuit.
#
#   net NAME: PIN ...     a supply rail
#   label NAME: PIN ...   a net MAME names
#   wire PIN PIN ...      an unnamed connection
#   port NAME: PIN ...    a net that leaves this file (see above)
#   nc PIN ...            a pin with nothing attached
#   parallel PIN ...      outputs the board sums on one node by design
#   value REF VALUE       a passive's value, in the unit MAME's own macro uses
#
# PIN is DESIGNATOR.NUMBER. Diode pin 1 is the cathode; transistors keep B, C and E;
# MAME does not record which way round an electrolytic goes, so C pins are MAME's 1/2.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Undone: what MAME does to simulate the board that the board does not do
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# line 27: #define HLE_SHOOT_VCO 1 -> 0 (high-level stand-in for a real circuit)
# line 28: #define SPLIT_SHARED_OSCILLATORS 1 -> 0 (one oscillator split in two for speed)
# line 29: #define ENABLE_SPIN_VCO_FRONTIER 1 -> 0 (solver partitioning only)
# line 30: #define ENABLE_NOISE_FRONTIERS 1 -> 0 (solver partitioning only)
# line 31: #define ENABLE_FRONTIERS 1 -> 0 (solver partitioning only)
# line 41: #define ADD_CLIPPING_DIODES 1 -> 0 (diodes standing in for the chip's own input clamps)
# line 619: NET_C(GND, R35.1, R35.2, C12.1, C12.2, U3.5, U3.9) -> nc -- parked on a rail with C12, R35 -- MAME replaces this circuit with a stand-in
# line 625: NET_C(GND, R6.1, R6.2, C11.1, C11.2, U3.1, U3.3) -> nc -- parked on a rail with C11, R6 -- MAME replaces this circuit with a stand-in
# line 631: NET_C(GND, R7.1, R7.2, C13.1, C13.2, U3.13, U3.11) -> nc -- parked on a rail with C13, R7 -- MAME replaces this circuit with a stand-in
# line 935: NET_C(GND, R138.1, R138.2, C61.1, C61.2, U19.1, U19.3) -> nc -- parked on a rail with C61, R138 -- MAME replaces this circuit with a stand-in
# line 941: NET_C(GND, R144.1, R144.2, C71.1, C71.2, U19.5, U19.9) -> nc -- parked on a rail with C71, R144 -- MAME replaces this circuit with a stand-in
# line 947: NET_C(GND, R139.1, R139.2, C62.1, C62.2, U19.13, U19.11) -> nc -- parked on a rail with C62, R139 -- MAME replaces this circuit with a stand-in
# line 1084: NET_C(GND, U21.5, U21.6) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unconnected inputs" block
# line 1085: NET_C(GND, U23.5, U23.6) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unconnected inputs" block
# Parked by MAME, both ends on a rail, because a stand-in replaces their circuit; on
# the board, not in this file: C11 0.01uF, C12 0.01uF, C13 0.01uF, C61 0.047uF, C62 0.047uF, C71 0.047uF, R6 680K, R7 680K, R35 680K, R138 150K, R139 150K, R144 220K
# line 198: R_PSG_1 is not a part -- a 1K from +5V standing in for one output of the sound chip (PSG) MAME emulates separately
# line 199: R_PSG_2 is not a part -- a 1K from +5V standing in for one output of the sound chip (PSG) MAME emulates separately
# line 200: R_PSG_3 is not a part -- a 1K from +5V standing in for one output of the sound chip (PSG) MAME emulates separately
# Stand-ins that are not parts (the nets they drive are ports): TTL_INPUT(I_LO_D0), TTL_INPUT(I_LO_D1), TTL_INPUT(I_LO_D2), TTL_INPUT(I_LO_D6), TTL_INPUT(I_LO_D7), TTL_INPUT(I_HI_D0), TTL_INPUT(I_HI_D1), TTL_INPUT(I_HI_D2), TTL_INPUT(I_HI_D3), TTL_INPUT(I_HI_D4), TTL_INPUT(I_HI_D5), CLOCK(O1CLK), CLOCK(O2CLK), CLOCK(O3CLK), CLOCK(O4CLK), CLOCK(O5CLK), CLOCK(O6CLK)
#
# Left out by MAME (commented out at TAG, so not in this file either):
#   line 207: RES(R1, RES_K(2.2))     -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 208: RES(R2, RES_K(10))      -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 209: RES(R4, RES_K(330))     -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 210: RES(R5, RES_M(1))       -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 220: RES(R15, RES_K(100))    -- part of final amp (not emulated)
